Focus: Stereotyping and equitable learning opportunities', 'Gold', 'Ask the affected student privately whether she wants support raising the allocation.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'Offering private support respects the affected student’s perspective and helps her decide how she wants to be involved in raising the repeated inequality. Direct challenge may also be appropriate, but this action meaningfully addresses the situation without creating a professional drawback.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Anonymous allegation, fairness and present safety', 'Gold', 'Forward the anonymous message only to the named peer and ask for an explanation before deciding whether to involve the supervisor.', '', '', '', 'Inappropriate, but not awful', 'Seeking the peer’s account recognises that the allegation may be false, but it delays a confidential fitness check before patient contact and alerts the subject before evidence can be assessed. The attempt at fairness prevents the lowest rating; relying on an unverified private explanation is unsafe.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Anonymous allegation, fairness and present safety', 'Gold', 'Send the message confidentially to the placement supervisor, state that Olivia cannot verify it and request a current fitness check without circulating the allegation further.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'Olivia neither endorses nor publicises the anonymous claim; she gives the responsible person enough information to assess an immediate risk proportionately. A confidential present-fitness check protects both patients and the accused peer, so the top rating is justified despite uncertainty about the historical allegation.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Deadlines, honesty and fair processes', 'Gold', 'Admit that he planned poorly, apologise and ask whether any legitimate late-submission process is available.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'Amir is honest, accepts responsibility and seeks only the legitimate process available to any student. The action directly protects fairness and introduces no competing ethical problem, so it merits the top rating.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Deadlines, honesty and fair processes', 'Gold', 'Submit the work late with a brief apology but no explanation.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'Submitting the work late with an apology is honest, accepts the ordinary consequence and makes no false claim for special treatment. Amir may choose to explain his poor planning separately, but the absence of an excuse is not an inherent defect in this action and should not lower the rating.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Immediate self-harm risk and confidentiality limits', 'Gold', 'Stay with Zain and encourage him to seek urgent help, but promise not to involve anyone without his permission.', '', '', '', 'Inappropriate, but not awful', 'Staying and encouraging help are constructive, but agreeing to withhold urgent assistance leaves the immediate risk inadequately managed. The action mishandles the issue, although it does not cross the clearer safety, honesty or rights threshold required for the lowest category.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Immediate self-harm risk and confidentiality limits', 'Diamond', 'Telephone Zain’s sibling to come immediately and stay with him, but do not contact urgent professional help unless the sibling agrees.', '', '', '', 'Inappropriate, but not awful', 'Bringing trusted support while Holly remains with Zain is constructive, but making urgent professional help depend on a relative’s agreement is inadequate for a specific, immediate risk. The attempt to avoid leaving him alone prevents the lowest rating, while the unsafe condition attached to escalation keeps it inappropriate.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Fair allocation and transparent criteria', 'Diamond', 'Use a transparent random ballot among all eligible applicants and publish the method in advance.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'With equal eligibility, a transparent ballot offers a fair and auditable process. Any sensible later monitoring is a separate step rather than a defect in this action, which supports the top category.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Fair allocation and transparent criteria', 'Diamond', 'Ask applicants to state relevant learning needs, then use published criteria and an independent reviewer.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'Published criteria tied to genuine learning needs, combined with independent review, create a transparent and defensible allocation process. A random ballot could also be appropriate under the supplied rules; independent actions can share the top rating when each fairly addresses the situation.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Near-miss learning and system improvement', 'Diamond', 'Correct the sheet transparently and tell the shift lead what happened, but leave the formal near-miss decision to them.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'The record is corrected transparently and the responsible shift lead receives the facts needed to decide and document the formal near-miss route. Leaving that procedural decision to the accountable lead is appropriate role discipline, not a failure to act, provided the student has reported the recurring abbreviation clearly as stated.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Near-miss learning and system improvement', 'Diamond', 'Submit a near-miss report about the unclear abbreviation but omit that the routine final check detected the error, because that detail seems reassuring.', '', '', '', 'Inappropriate, but not awful', 'Reporting the system problem is constructive, but deliberately omitting how the error was detected makes the account incomplete and weakens learning about which safeguards worked. The genuine report prevents the most severe rating; selective reporting keeps it inappropriate.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Assessment integrity and evidence preservation', 'Diamond', 'Leave the chat, avoid viewing the answers and preserve enough information to raise the issue through the proper route.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'Rebecca avoids benefiting from misconduct while enabling a fair response. Any sensible later monitoring is a separate step rather than a defect in this action, which supports the top category.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Assessment integrity and evidence preservation', 'Diamond', 'Tell the group to stop and leave immediately.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'Rebecca refuses participation and directly challenges ongoing misconduct before leaving. Reporting through the formal route may also be appropriate, but the action already addresses a central aspect safely; it should not be downgraded merely because another step could follow.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Patient complaint, support and fair process', 'Diamond', 'Tell the clinician privately what the patient reported and ask for their account before helping the patient obtain complaints information.', '', '', '', 'Appropriate, but not ideal', 'A private, non-accusatory conversation may provide useful context and is fairer than public confrontation. It is not ideal because access to the complaints process should not depend on Idris first informally investigating the allegation or accepting the clinician’s explanation.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Sharps injury and competing immediate duties', 'Diamond', 'Ask the trained colleague to secure the equipment while Beth immediately follows first aid and alerts the supervisor.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'Beth delegates the remaining environmental task to someone competent, allowing her to follow the urgent exposure process without leaving the area unsafe. The action resolves both duties promptly and proportionately, so it merits the top rating.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Sharps injury and competing immediate duties', 'Diamond', 'Wash the area immediately while asking the trained colleague to call the supervisor and occupational-health contact, then speak to them herself as soon as the call connects.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'Beth begins first aid without delay and uses a competent colleague to activate the required help while she is occupied. She remains personally involved in reporting rather than delegating responsibility, so the action handles both urgency and accountability fully.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Sharps injury and competing immediate duties', 'Diamond', 'Wash the puncture site immediately but wait until the current clearing task is complete before reporting the injury.', '', '', '', 'Inappropriate, but not awful', 'Immediate washing is beneficial, but delaying the stated reporting and assessment process is unsafe when another trained colleague can take over the clearing task. The prompt first-aid step prevents the lowest rating; avoidable delay keeps the overall action inappropriate.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Examination security and fair reporting', 'Diamond', 'Delete the message and file immediately without reporting them, so Chen cannot benefit from the material.', '', '', '', 'Inappropriate, but not awful', 'Deleting the material prevents Chen from using it, which is constructive, but it also destroys information the examination office may need to protect fairness for every candidate. The refusal to exploit the paper prevents the lowest rating, while failure to report and preserve evidence keeps it inappropriate.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Examination security and fair reporting', 'Diamond', 'Preserve the message without opening the file again and report it promptly through the appropriate examination route.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'This avoids further benefit, retains relevant evidence and allows the examination’s integrity to be protected. Nothing in the stated action creates delay, deception or role overreach, so ‘appropriate but not ideal’ would understate it.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Examination security and fair reporting', 'Diamond', 'Tell the friend not to send the file to anyone else.', '', '', '', 'Appropriate, but not ideal', 'Discouraging further circulation is helpful, but it does not ensure the existing breach reaches those able to act. This remains on the appropriate side because it helps, although the stated delay, assumption or incomplete handling prevents a ‘very appropriate’ rating.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Possible colleague impairment and compassionate escalation', 'Diamond', 'Ask Yara privately whether prescribed medication explains the signs and allow her to continue if she says it does.', '', '', '', 'Inappropriate, but not awful', 'A private question is respectful and may supply context, but a student cannot treat reassurance as a fitness assessment when Yara is confused, slurring and nearly falling. The attempt to understand rather than conceal the problem prevents the lowest rating; allowing patient contact without senior assessment keeps it inappropriate.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Possible colleague impairment and compassionate escalation', 'Diamond', 'Ask another colleague to stop the next patient entering while the student speaks to Yara privately and calls the senior clinician for immediate assessment.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'The student simultaneously prevents patient exposure, protects Yara’s dignity and obtains qualified assessment without attempting a diagnosis. Delegating the doorway task is proportionate and creates no material delay, so the action merits the top category.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Family pressure and autonomous decisions', 'Diamond', 'Suggest to the qualified clinician that speaking with the patient privately may help clarify her wishes.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'The student appropriately alerts the qualified clinician to a concrete sign of coercion and proposes a private conversation that could restore the patient’s voice. This is proportionate and within the student’s role, so it deserves the top rating even though the clinician must carry out the next step.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Family pressure and autonomous decisions', 'Diamond', 'Ask the relatives to describe their practical concerns, then suggest that the clinician speaks with the patient alone before any decision is made.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'The action recognises that relatives may hold useful practical information while preserving the capable patient’s right to decide free from pressure. It does not give the family authority over treatment and explicitly secures a private conversation, so it is very appropriate.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Family pressure and autonomous decisions', 'Diamond', 'Tell the patient that her relatives’ views deserve substantial weight because they provide daily support, then ask whether she will reconsider.', '', '', '', 'Inappropriate, but not awful', 'Practical support is relevant, but presenting the relatives’ preference as a reason to reverse a capable patient’s refusal adds pressure and risks undermining voluntariness. The action stops short of overriding her decision, which prevents the lowest rating, but it remains inappropriate.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Research withdrawal and accurate information', 'Diamond', 'Acknowledge the request, stop further participation and follow the stated withdrawal process.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'This respects the participant’s stated right and applies the supplied process without pressure. Any sensible later monitoring is a separate step rather than a defect in this action, which supports the top category.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Research withdrawal and accurate information', 'Diamond', 'Ask once whether the participant would like information about what withdrawal involves before confirming the request.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'Anya offers relevant information once so the participant can understand what withdrawal means, while leaving the decision with him. The action is not coercive and can prevent misunderstanding, so it is very appropriate; repeated persuasion would be different.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Research withdrawal and accurate information', 'Diamond', 'Record withdrawal from future participation immediately, explain that Anya must check the separate rules before answering about existing data and arrange prompt follow-up.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'Anya implements the unambiguous part of the request at once while refusing to guess about data already collected. The clarification is prompt and does not condition or delay withdrawal, so the action respects autonomy and accuracy fully.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Record error, patient check and independent reporting', 'Diamond', 'Correct the record transparently and ask another qualified clinician to check the patient, but rely on the original senior clinician to submit the formal report.', '', '', '', 'Appropriate, but not ideal', 'The action protects the patient and preserves record integrity, so it is clearly constructive. It is not ideal because the senior has already requested concealment; Malik should ensure that the required report is made rather than rely on that same person to complete it.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Record error, patient check and independent reporting', 'Diamond', 'Immediately contact an appropriate qualified clinician who can check the patient, while preserving the original entry and following the reporting process.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'This correctly prioritises possible patient impact, transparent records and formal follow-up. Nothing in the stated action creates delay, deception or role overreach, so ‘appropriate but not ideal’ would understate it.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Record error, patient check and independent reporting', 'Diamond', 'Tell the senior clinician clearly that Malik will follow the local process, then contact another qualified clinician without continuing the argument.', '', '', '', 'A very appropriate thing to do', 'Malik challenges the improper instruction without seeking permission and moves promptly to an independent clinician who can protect the patient. Ending the debate avoids hierarchy causing further delay, so the response is decisive, proportionate and within his role.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Record error, patient check and independent reporting', 'Diamond', 'Document the correction but describe it only as a ‘technical issue’, without recording that the result was entered in the wrong patient’s record.', '', '', '', 'Inappropriate, but not awful', 'Recording that a correction occurred is better than deleting the evidence, but the vague description conceals the nature and potential consequence of the error. The partial audit trail prevents the lowest rating, while misleading incompleteness keeps the action inappropriate.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Confidentiality and information handling', 'Bronze', 'Whether an unauthorised person could see the information if the screen remains open.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'The immediate risk of an avoidable confidentiality breach is vital when deciding whether to act at once. The core professional choice cannot be made reliably without it, making the lower adjacent category too weak.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Feedback, empathy and respectful support', 'Bronze', 'Whether Mei felt humiliated by receiving the feedback publicly.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'The effect of the tutor’s manner is materially relevant, although Arun must not assume misconduct without understanding the exchange. It should materially shape the response, but the central duty would remain even if this detail changed, so ‘very important’ would overstate it.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Reliability, communication and practical support', 'Bronze', 'Whether Joel produces higher-quality work than every other group member.', '', '', '', 'Of minor importance', 'His contribution may affect how the group supports him, but it does not remove the disruption caused by repeated lateness. It can be noticed without driving the decision, which distinguishes minor importance from the adjacent ‘important’ category.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Confidentiality and information handling', 'Bronze', 'Whether the image would make Nadia’s revision notes more visually interesting.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Personal convenience or interest has no legitimate weight against privacy and permission. No legitimate professional decision turns on this detail, so even ‘of minor importance’ would give it undeserved weight.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Professional identification and reliability', 'Bronze', 'Whether patients and staff can verify Tomas’s identity and student status.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'Clear identification protects trust, security and informed interaction with a student. The core professional choice cannot be made reliably without it, making the lower adjacent category too weak.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Dignity, discrimination and respectful challenge', 'Bronze', 'The possible effect of the remark on colleagues who heard it.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Impact is materially relevant even if the speaker claims no offence was intended. It should materially shape the response, but the central duty would remain even if this detail changed, so ‘very important’ would overstate it.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Knowing limits and seeking supervision', 'Bronze', 'Whether refusing might make the clinician think Farah lacks confidence.', '', '', '', 'Of minor importance', 'The impression she makes may concern her personally, but it should carry little weight compared with competence and safety. It can be noticed without driving the decision, which distinguishes minor importance from the adjacent ‘important’ category.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Attendance, integrity and accurate records', 'Bronze', 'Whether Owen wants his friend to remain pleased with him.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Preserving approval is not a legitimate consideration when asked to participate in dishonesty. No legitimate professional decision turns on this detail, so even ‘of minor importance’ would give it undeserved weight.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Honest communication within role limits', 'Bronze', 'The risk that an unsupported answer could cause serious distress or false reassurance.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'Potential harm from misinformation is central to deciding not to guess. The core professional choice cannot be made reliably without it, making the lower adjacent category too weak.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Reliability and early communication', 'Bronze', 'Whether staff need to reorganise an activity because Kai is absent.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'The practical effect on others is materially relevant to how quickly and clearly he should communicate. It should materially shape the response, but the central duty would remain even if this detail changed, so ‘very important’ would overstate it.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Patient safety and speaking up', 'Bronze', 'Whether Mina has previously seen this nurse make a mistake.', '', '', '', 'Of minor importance', 'The visible mismatch requires checking regardless of the nurse’s previous record. Some contextual value remains, but the response should be essentially unchanged if this factor were different.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Transparent correction of records', 'Bronze', 'Whether the original incorrect value made Elias’s work look more impressive.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Personal advantage must not influence whether an inaccurate record is corrected transparently. The consideration has no proper connection to safety, honesty, rights or proportionality and should not influence the response at all.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Patient confidentiality and family requests', 'Bronze', 'The patient’s explicit instruction not to share information with relatives.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'The patient’s stated preference is vital unless an exceptional overriding reason is supplied. It is a decision-changing factor rather than useful background, which rules out the adjacent ‘important’ rating.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Choice, consent and dignity', 'Bronze', 'The effect that student presence may have on the patient’s comfort.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Comfort and voluntary agreement materially affect whether student participation is appropriate. It should materially shape the response, but the central duty would remain even if this detail changed, so ‘very important’ would overstate it.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Listening, de-escalation and managing complaints', 'Bronze', 'Whether other patients have complained as loudly.', '', '', '', 'Of minor importance', 'Other reactions may provide context but should not determine whether this patient receives a respectful and useful response. Some contextual value remains, but the response should be essentially unchanged if this factor were different.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Supporting a struggling colleague safely', 'Bronze', 'Whether helping Dev will make Amina appear more generous to the supervisor.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Personal appearance should not influence a decision about a colleague’s welfare and safe workload. The consideration has no proper connection to safety, honesty, rights or proportionality and should not influence the response at all.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Raising an unresolved safety concern', 'Bronze', 'The possibility that information could be filed under the wrong person.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'The direct risk created by the mixed documents is vital to deciding whether immediate checking or escalation is required. It is a decision-changing factor rather than useful background, which rules out the adjacent ‘important’ rating.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Scope of practice and supervision', 'Bronze', 'Whether Rosa has been assessed as competent to perform the procedure without supervision.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'Whether Rosa has been assessed as competent is central to deciding what she can safely undertake and what supervision is required. Ignoring this could change the safe decision, so describing it as merely important would be too weak.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Discrimination, dignity and fair treatment', 'Bronze', 'Whether the patient used polite language before making the discriminatory remark.', '', '', '', 'Of minor importance', 'Tone may slightly affect how the conversation is managed, but it does not change the discriminatory content. Some contextual value remains, but the response should be essentially unchanged if this factor were different.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Gifts and professional boundaries', 'Bronze', 'Whether chocolate is Lina’s favourite food.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Personal preference has no legitimate bearing on the professional boundary decision. The consideration has no proper connection to safety, honesty, rights or proportionality and should not influence the response at all.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Fatigue, honesty and safe participation', 'Silver', 'Whether Marcus’s fatigue resulted from an avoidable choice rather than an unavoidable illness.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'The cause does not change the immediate need to assess fitness, but it does affect honest accountability, later reflection and what support or follow-up is proportionate. It therefore matters without being the vital determinant of whether Marcus should continue patient-facing activity now.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Plagiarism and shared accountability', 'Silver', 'The effect that plagiarism could have on every named group member.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Shared academic and reputational consequences materially strengthen the need to resolve the problem. It should materially shape the response, but the central duty would remain even if this detail changed, so ‘very important’ would overstate it.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Misdirected confidential information', 'Silver', 'Whether the sender may feel embarrassed after being told about the mistake.', '', '', '', 'Of minor importance', 'Embarrassment may influence Noor’s tact, but should have little effect on reporting and protecting the information. Some contextual value remains, but the response should be essentially unchanged if this factor were different.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Online confidentiality and indirect identification', 'Silver', 'Whether Theo’s educational purpose creates a legitimate reason to explore a properly authorised and de-identified version of the case.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'A genuine educational benefit may justify seeking permission or developing a safely anonymised version rather than abandoning all teaching use. It does not reduce the present identification risk or authorise publication, so it is relevant but not decisive.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Interpretation, consent and privacy', 'Silver', 'Whether the patient can understand the information and express her own decision accurately.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'Meaningful understanding and communication are vital to valid consent. It is a decision-changing factor rather than useful background, which rules out the adjacent ‘important’ rating.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Research integrity and limitations', 'Silver', 'Whether the missing values could materially change the project’s conclusion.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'The possible effect on interpretation is relevant, although missing data must not be invented regardless of effect. Ignoring it would weaken the decision, although other stated duties still control the final choice, so the highest rating is too strong.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Research integrity and limitations', 'Silver', 'Whether explaining which values are missing and how that limits the conclusion will allow the marker to judge the evidence accurately.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Transparent explanation materially helps the reader interpret the project and distinguishes honest missing data from selective reporting. It is important rather than vital because the values must not be invented regardless of how strongly they affect the conclusion.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Infection-control uncertainty and escalation', 'Silver', 'Whether setting the instrument aside may delay the procedure by several minutes.', '', '', '', 'Of minor importance', 'A short delay may affect workflow and should be communicated, but it should carry little weight until the instrument’s safety is confirmed. Calling it important would give convenience too much influence over a potential infection-control risk.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Infection-control uncertainty and escalation', 'Silver', 'Whether the instrument’s status can be confirmed before patient contact.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'Verification before use is vital to removing the potential safety risk. Because it determines the safe or ethical direction of the response, it deserves the highest importance category.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Repeated discrimination and proportionate escalation', 'Silver', 'Whether the behaviour has continued after Asha asked for it to stop.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Repetition shows that informal correction has failed and strengthens the case for support and escalation. The factor deserves genuine weight without becoming independently decisive, placing it below the top importance category.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Repeated discrimination and proportionate escalation', 'Silver', 'Whether the laughter of other students may make Asha feel unable to challenge the behaviour again herself.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'The group response may increase isolation and reduce Asha’s ability to address the problem without support. It should influence the response, but the repeated mockery already warrants action even if she still feels able to speak, so it is not independently vital.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Appointment errors and transparent correction', 'Silver', 'Whether Finn noticed the error before anybody acted on the incorrect appointment date.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Early discovery reduces the likelihood that harm has already occurred and affects what follow-up may be needed. It does not remove the need for a transparent correction, so it is important rather than decisive.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Appointment errors and transparent correction', 'Silver', 'The possible consequence of the patient receiving the wrong appointment information.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'The direct practical effect is vital to understanding why the mistake requires immediate correction. It is a decision-changing factor rather than useful background, which rules out the adjacent ‘important’ rating.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Acute distress and seeking appropriate help', 'Silver', 'Whether Jay wants Salma to involve the nearby tutor.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'His preference matters, although an apparent urgent welfare risk could still require help despite reluctance. Ignoring it would weaken the decision, although other stated duties still control the final choice, so the highest rating is too strong.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Acute distress and seeking appropriate help', 'Silver', 'Whether Jay has previously appeared mildly nervous before assessments.', '', '', '', 'Of minor importance', 'Previous nerves provide limited context, but the severity of his current distress should determine the response. It may refine tone or later reflection, but it should not materially alter the immediate professional choice, so ‘important’ would be too strong.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Possible impairment and immediate patient safety', 'Silver', 'Whether reporting the concern may damage their friendship.', '', '', '', 'Of minor importance', 'Possible damage to the friendship may affect how sensitively Niko speaks and whether he seeks support afterwards. It must not determine whether a credible immediate safety concern is escalated, so giving it substantial weight would be inappropriate.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Possible impairment and immediate patient safety', 'Silver', 'The risk that she may participate in patient care while impaired.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'Preventing potentially unsafe patient contact is the vital consideration. Because it determines the safe or ethical direction of the response, it deserves the highest importance category.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Fair credit and evidence-based challenge', 'Silver', 'Whether the guide was genuinely created through shared work.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Authorship evidence is materially relevant to correcting credit and deciding whether dishonesty occurred. The factor deserves genuine weight without becoming independently decisive, placing it below the top importance category.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Fair credit and evidence-based challenge', 'Silver', 'Whether Adam may genuinely believe that compiling and formatting the final version entitled him to sole authorship.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'His understanding is relevant to the tone of the first conversation and to whether the problem began as deliberate dishonesty or a mistaken view of contribution. It cannot settle authorship against the shared evidence, so it is important but not vital.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Accessibility and equal participation', 'Silver', 'Whether receiving notes afterwards offers Mariam the same opportunity to observe demonstrations, ask questions and participate.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'The proposed alternative must be judged by whether it provides genuinely equivalent access, not merely some information. Because this determines whether Mariam remains excluded from mandatory teaching, it is a vital consideration.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Accessibility and equal participation', 'Silver', 'Whether changing rooms would reduce the available teaching time by about ten minutes.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Lost teaching time is a genuine practical cost and should shape how efficiently the group moves or whether an equivalent live arrangement is better. It cannot justify excluding Mariam from mandatory participation, so it is relevant but not vital.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Allergy information and timely escalation', 'Silver', 'Whether the receiving clinician may already have seen the allergy alert elsewhere in the record.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Existing awareness is relevant to urgency, but Elif should not assume it and must still ensure the omission is corrected. The factor deserves genuine weight without becoming independently decisive, placing it below the top importance category.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Possible medication discrepancy and role limits', 'Silver', 'Whether the different appearance could have an innocent explanation.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'An innocent explanation is relevant because George should raise the discrepancy without accusing anyone or alarming the patient unnecessarily. It must not delay checking, so it is important to the manner of response but not vital to whether the concern is acted on.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

