Focus: Public conversation and identifiability', 'Gold', 'The likelihood that visitors can identify which patient is being discussed.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'Identifiability is vital when assessing the immediacy and seriousness of the confidentiality risk. It is a decision-changing factor rather than useful background, which rules out the adjacent ‘important’ rating.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Family interpretation and voluntary communication', 'Gold', 'Whether the discussion includes information the patient may not want her daughter to hear.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'The patient’s hesitation and the sensitive subject make the possibility of unwanted disclosure central to choosing an interpreter. Ignoring it could prevent the patient speaking freely, so the consideration is vital rather than merely important.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Bereavement, empathy and role limits', 'Gold', 'Whether Cora will be late for her next activity.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Cora has a real responsibility to the next activity, so it should influence how quickly she arranges a clear handover rather than trying to manage the conversation alone. It is not vital because the bereaved relative must not be abandoned simply to protect punctuality.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Conflict, de-escalation and urgent work', 'Gold', 'Whether one student appears to have started the argument.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Responsibility is relevant to the later fair resolution of the dispute, but it should not control the immediate need to de-escalate, protect the environment and complete urgent work. It therefore matters without being the vital first consideration.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Near misses, hierarchy and speaking up', 'Gold', 'Whether reporting against the senior clinician’s instruction may damage Ibrahim’s working relationship with the person assessing him.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'The assessor relationship does not change the duty to report, but it materially affects which independent route, support and documentation Ibrahim may need to act safely. It therefore deserves real weight in planning the response, though patient safety and honest reporting remain decisive.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Repeated safety failures and proportional escalation', 'Gold', 'Whether the omission has occurred repeatedly after feedback.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'Recurrence after feedback shows that a one-off reminder has not resolved the behaviour and directly changes the proportional level of escalation required. Because ignoring the pattern could allow repeated safety failures, the consideration is vital.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Online patient contact and boundaries', 'Gold', 'Whether declining without explanation may leave the person feeling rejected.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'The person’s likely experience should influence Ellie’s tone and whether she redirects them to an appropriate service channel. It cannot justify accepting the personal request or giving advice, so it is important but not vital to the boundary decision.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Attraction, impartiality and professional boundaries', 'Gold', 'Whether Daniel can continue to behave impartially without seeking additional contact with the person.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'His ability to maintain ordinary professional conduct determines whether simple self-management is sufficient or whether changes and guidance are needed. Because it directly affects boundary protection and fair care, it is vital.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Infection risk, attendance and early notice', 'Gold', 'Whether the assessed activity will be difficult to rearrange if Sophie gives late notice.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'The practical consequence should encourage prompt communication and helps the placement manage fairness and resources. It cannot justify attending against the explicit exclusion rule, so it is important to how Sophie responds rather than vital to whether she stays away.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Stereotyping and equitable learning opportunities', 'Gold', 'Whether the allocation repeatedly denies one student equivalent learning opportunities.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Unequal educational impact materially increases the seriousness beyond a single clumsy comment. It should materially shape the response, but the central duty would remain even if this detail changed, so ‘very important’ would overstate it.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Stereotyping and equitable learning opportunities', 'Gold', 'Whether Max believes the stereotype was complimentary.', '', '', '', 'Of minor importance', 'Intention may affect how to start the conversation, but it does little to reduce the unequal impact. The detail is not wholly irrelevant, yet giving it substantial weight would displace the real issue and overrate its significance.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Anonymous allegation, fairness and present safety', 'Gold', 'Whether the specific date and location can be checked confidentially without circulating the allegation among students.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Verifiable detail supports a proportionate factual check and reduces reliance on an unsupported accusation. It is important rather than vital because the possibility of immediate impairment still warrants a confidential fitness check even if the historical claim cannot be confirmed.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Anonymous allegation, fairness and present safety', 'Gold', 'Whether the supervisor can check the peer’s current fitness without treating the anonymous historical allegation as proven.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'This determines whether Olivia can protect patients while also avoiding an unsupported accusation or unnecessary disclosure. A route that separates present safety assessment from a finding of past intoxication is decision-changing, so the consideration is vital rather than merely useful.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Deadlines, honesty and fair processes', 'Gold', 'Whether the tutor needs accurate information to apply deadline rules fairly.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Fair and consistent decision-making depends materially on truthful circumstances. It should materially shape the response, but the central duty would remain even if this detail changed, so ‘very important’ would overstate it.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Deadlines, honesty and fair processes', 'Gold', 'Whether seeing peers miss deadlines contributed to Amir treating the deadline less seriously.', '', '', '', 'Of minor importance', 'This may help him reflect on how the problem developed, but should have little influence on the immediate honest response. The detail is not wholly irrelevant, yet giving it substantial weight would displace the real issue and overrate its significance.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Immediate self-harm risk and confidentiality limits', 'Diamond', 'Whether obtaining urgent help may temporarily damage Zain’s trust in Holly.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Trust matters because it affects how Holly communicates, stays with Zain and supports him after help arrives. It cannot outweigh the specific immediate risk, so it is important to the manner of intervention but not vital to whether urgent assistance is obtained.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Immediate self-harm risk and confidentiality limits', 'Diamond', 'Whether Zain’s previous poor experience means involving a trusted adult alongside urgent professional support may help him engage with that support.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Past experience and trusted support should materially shape how urgent help is introduced and sustained. They cannot reduce the need for professional assistance given the specific immediate plan, so the factor is important to engagement but not the decisive safety threshold.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Fair allocation and transparent criteria', 'Diamond', 'Whether the allocation method can be explained consistently to unsuccessful applicants.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Transparency and consistency materially support fairness and trust. It should materially shape the response, but the central duty would remain even if this detail changed, so ‘very important’ would overstate it.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Fair allocation and transparent criteria', 'Diamond', 'Whether some applicants have relevant learning needs even though the current rules give nobody automatic priority.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Relevant need may justify considering transparent criteria rather than assuming every candidate is identically placed. It is not vital because, without an established priority rule, a fair ballot could also be defensible.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Near-miss learning and system improvement', 'Diamond', 'Whether the wrong-side error was detected by the intended routine check rather than only by chance.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'How the error was found helps the team judge whether the safety system worked and which part of the process needs improvement. It should influence the review, but it does not remove the need to learn from the near miss, so it is not vital.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Near-miss learning and system improvement', 'Diamond', 'Whether the same unclear abbreviation appears on unused forms that could expose other teams to a similar error before the next routine review.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'A continuing system hazard changes the issue from a completed isolated near miss to a preventable risk for future patients. Because that fact can alter the urgency and scope of corrective action, describing it as merely important would be too weak.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Assessment integrity and evidence preservation', 'Diamond', 'Whether remaining in the chat briefly to preserve evidence would risk Rebecca receiving or appearing to use additional answers.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Evidence may help a fair investigation, but continued exposure could compromise Rebecca’s own assessment position and allow more answers to load. This trade-off should shape how she preserves only what is already visible and exits promptly, though it does not change the need to avoid using the material and report appropriately.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Assessment integrity and evidence preservation', 'Diamond', 'Whether the filenames could be misleading and some students in the chat may not have opened or used the attachments.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Uncertainty matters because Rebecca should report observed facts rather than label every participant a cheat. It does not make the live sharing allegation irrelevant or justify silence, so it is important to fairness and wording but not decisive against reporting.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Patient complaint, support and fair process', 'Diamond', 'Whether Idris’s previous positive experience of the clinician differs from the patient’s account.', '', '', '', 'Of minor importance', 'The difference reminds Idris that he has incomplete information and should not declare either account proven. It should have little influence on whether the patient is heard and given access to the complaint route, so it remains a minor contextual factor.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Patient complaint, support and fair process', 'Diamond', 'Whether the patient wants practical support now or only accurate information about the complaints route.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Her preference should shape whether Idris accompanies her, finds somebody immediately or simply provides the route without taking over. It does not determine whether she is entitled to accurate information, so it is important rather than vital.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Sharps injury and competing immediate duties', 'Diamond', 'Whether the trained colleague can secure the remaining equipment safely without Beth.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Available competent cover removes a practical obstacle to Beth leaving the task immediately and should shape the handover. Even without it, the exposure instructions would still require urgent assistance and another safe arrangement, so the consideration is important rather than vital.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Sharps injury and competing immediate duties', 'Diamond', 'Whether embarrassment could cause Beth to minimise the timing or circumstances of the injury when she reports it.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Accurate facts may affect the assistance, documentation and later learning, so Beth’s emotional response deserves attention and supportive communication. Embarrassment does not change the need for immediate first aid and assessment, making it important but not vital.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Examination security and fair reporting', 'Diamond', 'Whether Chen can prove that the file is genuine without opening more of it.', '', '', '', 'Of minor importance', 'Authenticity affects the examination office’s eventual investigation, but Chen should not inspect more potentially leaked material to establish it himself. The current title and sender’s claim are enough to justify confidential reporting, so proof has little weight in his immediate decision.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Examination security and fair reporting', 'Diamond', 'Whether the examination office can assess and mitigate the possible leak without Chen proving authenticity by opening more of the file.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'This supports a proportionate division of roles: Chen can preserve what he already received while the authorised office investigates and protects fairness. The possibility does not determine whether he reports, but it materially explains why further personal inspection is unnecessary.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Possible colleague impairment and compassionate escalation', 'Diamond', 'Yara’s previously strong performance.', '', '', '', 'Of minor importance', 'Yara’s usual competence suggests the change may be acute and should encourage a respectful, non-accusatory approach. It should not materially alter the need to stop patient contact and obtain assessment for the signs present now, so giving it full importance would be too much weight.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Possible colleague impairment and compassionate escalation', 'Diamond', 'Whether Yara may feel embarrassed when help is called.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Yara’s dignity should meaningfully shape where, how and by whom she is approached, particularly because the cause is unknown. It cannot justify delay or continued patient contact, so it is important but not vital to whether help is obtained.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Family pressure and autonomous decisions', 'Diamond', 'Whether the relatives usually help the patient understand information and manage care at home.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'Their usual supportive role may help the clinician communicate and plan care with the patient’s permission. It does not transfer decision-making authority or justify pressure, so it is important context but not the vital determinant.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Family pressure and autonomous decisions', 'Diamond', 'Whether the patient can express her preference free from pressure.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'Voluntary expression of the patient’s own decision is vital. It is a decision-changing factor rather than useful background, which rules out the adjacent ‘important’ rating.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Research withdrawal and accurate information', 'Diamond', 'What the information sheet says about handling data already collected.', '', '', '', 'Very important', 'The information sheet defines what was promised about already collected data and is essential to answering the participant accurately and implementing withdrawal. Because guessing could misrepresent his rights, the consideration is vital.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Research withdrawal and accurate information', 'Diamond', 'Whether the participant’s reason reveals a minor inconvenience that the study could improve for future participants.', '', '', '', 'Of minor importance', 'The information may modestly improve future study design, but it should have little influence on honouring the withdrawal. It can be noticed without driving the decision, which distinguishes minor importance from the adjacent ‘important’ category.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Record error, patient check and independent reporting', 'Diamond', 'Whether the senior clinician’s instruction and assessment role may make Malik need support to use an independent reporting route.', '', '', '', 'Important', 'The power imbalance is relevant to how Malik can act safely and may justify seeking another qualified clinician or confidential support. It does not change the need to protect the patient and report transparently, so it is important but not vital to the underlying duty.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Reliability, communication and practical support', 'Bronze', 'Select one most appropriate action and one least appropriate action.', 'Speak with Joel privately, describe the disruption and ask whether a practical difficulty is affecting his attendance.', 'Change the next meeting time once without discussing the repeated lateness with Joel.', 'Make a sarcastic comment about Joel’s timekeeping in front of the group.', 'most:0|least:2', 'A addresses the repeated problem directly, respectfully and with enough curiosity to identify support that may be needed. B may reduce one immediate clash but avoids the pattern. C is least appropriate because public sarcasm humiliates Joel and is unlikely to produce a reliable solution.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Patient safety and speaking up', 'Bronze', 'Select one most appropriate action and one least appropriate action.', 'Say nothing because challenging a qualified professional could appear disrespectful.', 'Calmly ask the nurse to pause and check the patient name on the label before taking the medicine into the bay.', 'Ask another student whether the label looks wrong before deciding whether to alert the nurse.', 'most:1|least:0', 'B is most appropriate because it interrupts a specific potential safety error without accusing the nurse or pretending to know the explanation. C shows concern but creates avoidable delay. A is least appropriate because deference is allowed to override an immediate, preventable risk.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Listening, de-escalation and managing complaints', 'Bronze', 'Select one most appropriate action and one least appropriate action.', 'Explain that other patients have also been waiting and ask him to be patient.', 'Warn that continued complaining may result in him being asked to leave.', 'Acknowledge the patient’s frustration, ask what information would help now and contact the receptionist for an update.', 'most:2|least:1', 'C is most appropriate because it listens, stays within Safa’s role and obtains useful help. A is dismissive but offers some context. B is least appropriate because it uses an unjustified threat that may silence a legitimate concern and escalate the encounter.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Plagiarism and shared accountability', 'Silver', 'Select one most appropriate action and one least appropriate action.', 'Tell the friend that every copied section must be removed or referenced, help identify the affected passages and seek an honest extension if correction cannot be completed safely.', 'Send the copied passages to the tutor immediately and ask the tutor to resolve the matter, without first telling the friend or the rest of the group.', 'Quietly delete the copied passages from the shared draft and submit the shortened assignment without telling the group why material disappeared.', 'most:0|least:2', 'A is most appropriate because it prevents plagiarism, supports correction and preserves an honest route if time runs out. B protects integrity but escalates before giving the group a reasonable opportunity to correct the draft. C is least appropriate because, although it removes copied text, it unilaterally alters shared work and conceals the underlying problem.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Repeated discrimination and proportionate escalation', 'Silver', 'Select one most appropriate action and one least appropriate action.', 'Tell the student privately after the session that the comments are unacceptable, must stop and will be raised with the tutor if they recur.', 'Check that Asha is supported and report the repeated behaviour to the tutor, involving Asha in how this is done where possible.', 'Check that Asha is all right and follow her preference not to report today, even though the earlier request to stop has failed.', 'most:1|least:2', 'B is most appropriate because it combines support with proportionate escalation after a repeated pattern has resisted direct correction. A challenges the behaviour but postpones escalation once again. C is least appropriate because supporting Asha is helpful, yet treating her reluctance as a reason for complete inaction leaves a witnessed, repeated problem unaddressed.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Fair credit and evidence-based challenge', 'Silver', 'Select one most appropriate action and one least appropriate action.', 'Ask the tutor to delay featuring the guide while the contributors clarify authorship, without publicly accusing Adam.', 'Ask Adam to list all four students as equal authors immediately because the edit history shows that each contributed something.', 'Review the edit history, speak to Adam privately about proportionate credit and involve the tutor if an accurate correction cannot be agreed.', 'most:2|least:1', 'C is most appropriate because it uses evidence, allows a fair direct correction and retains proportionate escalation. A protects against premature publication but does not itself resolve credit. B is least appropriate because it replaces one unsupported authorship claim with an assumption that every contribution was equal, even though the edit history has not yet been evaluated.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Public conversation and identifiability', 'Gold', 'Select one most appropriate action and one least appropriate action.', 'Quietly ask the staff members to pause because people in the lift may identify the patient from the combined details.', 'Wait until the lift doors open, then ask the staff to continue the discussion in a private area and explain that visitors may have overheard.', 'Say, ‘Could we continue this somewhere private?’ without repeating any clinical details or naming confidentiality in front of the visitors.', 'most:0|least:1', 'A is most appropriate because it stops the active disclosure promptly and discreetly while making the reason clear enough to change behaviour. C also stops the conversation and avoids amplifying the details, but is less explicit. B is least appropriate because its later feedback is constructive yet permits the disclosure to continue for the remainder of the lift journey.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Conflict, de-escalation and urgent work', 'Gold', 'Select one most appropriate action and one least appropriate action.', 'Ask the group leader to take over the disagreement immediately while Leanne completes the urgent task herself.', 'Ask both students to pause, move the discussion away from patients and complete the urgent work before reviewing the disagreement privately.', 'Ask only the louder student to lower their voice and leave the underlying dispute for the group leader later.', 'most:1|least:2', 'B is most appropriate because it addresses the public disruption, protects urgent work and avoids prejudging blame. A obtains authority and safeguards the task, but may leave the argument audible while help is found and takes work away from both participants. C is least appropriate because it singles out one person and reduces noise without reliably ending the dispute or securing the urgent task.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Attraction, impartiality and professional boundaries', 'Gold', 'Select one most appropriate action and one least appropriate action.', 'Decline contact during placement but say he may reconsider coffee once the person is discharged from the service.', 'Swap one non-essential task with a peer to reduce contact while he arranges confidential guidance, without sharing the person’s details.', 'Maintain ordinary professional behaviour, avoid unnecessary contact and seek confidential guidance before responding to the invitation.', 'most:2|least:0', 'C is most appropriate because it manages both conduct and the unanswered invitation without exploiting the care relationship or overreacting to the feeling itself. B is a defensible temporary safeguard but may alter work unnecessarily before guidance. A is least appropriate because it preserves the prospect of a personal relationship created through care and signals future availability before the boundary has been properly assessed.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Patient complaint, support and fair process', 'Diamond', 'Select one most appropriate action and one least appropriate action.', 'Tell the clinician privately what was reported and ask for their account before offering the patient information about making a complaint.', 'Listen without deciding whether the allegation is true and arrange for the patient to receive accurate information about the complaints process.', 'Ask what support the patient wants, find an appropriate staff member to explain the complaints route and offer to accompany her if she wishes.', 'most:2|least:0', 'C is most appropriate because it preserves the patient’s control, secures accurate help and does not require Idris to decide the allegation. B is also fair and helpful but assumes an arrangement before clarifying what support the patient wants. A is least appropriate because a private account may add context, yet it makes access to the complaints route depend on Idris informally investigating the clinician first.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Possible colleague impairment and compassionate escalation', 'Diamond', 'Select one most appropriate action and one least appropriate action.', 'Arrange cover for the clinic and let Yara travel home alone if she says she can manage, without involving a senior clinician.', 'Prevent Yara seeing the next patient, obtain senior help immediately and make sure she is assessed compassionately.', 'Ask Yara to sit somewhere private, arrange cover and offer to contact the senior clinician with her, informing the senior anyway if she refuses.', 'most:1|least:0', 'B is most appropriate because it gives the quickest reliable protection and assessment for both Yara and patients. C is compassionate and ultimately ensures escalation, but adds a negotiation step despite serious signs. A is least appropriate because cover protects patients, yet an acutely confused person who nearly fell is allowed to leave unassessed and alone.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

Focus: Record error, patient check and independent reporting', 'Diamond', 'Select one most appropriate action and one least appropriate action.', 'Contact another qualified clinician immediately, preserve the original entry, correct it transparently and follow the reporting process.', 'Preserve the entry and ask the original senior to check the patient first, reporting only if harm is found or the senior agrees.', 'Correct the record transparently, tell the senior that Malik will submit the required report and ask another qualified clinician to check the patient.', 'most:0|least:1', 'A is most appropriate because it does not rely on the clinician who requested concealment and addresses safety, record integrity and reporting without delay. C is also strong but first re-engages the pressuring senior, which may complicate urgent action. B is least appropriate because preserving the entry is useful, yet assessment and reporting remain controlled by the person who has already opposed transparency.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

